Haesung A. Lee obtained his B.S. in Chemistry and Biological Sciences from KAIST in 2015 and is a Ph.D. candidate in the group of Prof. Haeshin Lee. His research interests include polyphenol-conjugated biopolymers and their applications.
Yanfei Ma received his B.S. in chemistry from Northwest Normal University in China in 2015. He is currently a Ph.D. candidate in the group of Prof. Feng Zhou at the Lanzhou Institute of Chemical Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences. His research interests include wet friction/adhesion control of soft matter and bionic adhesion.
Feng Zhou is a Professor at the State Key Laboratory of Solid Lubrication at the Lanzhou Institute of Chemical Physics and an adjunct professor at Northwestern Polytechnical University. He got his Ph.D. in 2004 from the Lanzhou Institute of Chemical Physics. He spent three years (2005−2008) in the Department of Chemistry at the University of Cambridge as a research associate. His research interests include surfaces and interfaces of soft matter, drag reduction and antifouling, and biolubrication.
Seonki Hong is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Emerging Materials Science at DGIST. She pursued her Ph.D. studies in the Department of Chemistry at KAIST and worked as a postdoctoral research fellow at Massachusetts General Hospital and Harvard Medical School. Her research interests have been focused on the design of innovative molecular glues/adhesives by mimicking the chemical structures of unique natural polyphenolic materials and the development of point-of-care bioassays for the precise detection of circulating biomarkers by utilizing these molecular glues.
Haeshin Lee is Professor in the Department of Chemistry at KAIST. He obtained his Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering from Northwestern University in 2008. He invented polydopamine coating in 2007 with P. B. Messersmith. His research interests include bioinspired chemistry of catechol and gallol derivatives, adhesive hydrogels and sols, and drug delivery systems. Currently he is an associate editor of Biomaterials Science.
